{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Iterator","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure","externalID":"s:7Cliques07MaximalA0V8IteratorV","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Iterator","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MaximalCliques.Iterator","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques.swift#L273","fileName":"MaximalCliques.swift"},"modules":[{"name":"Cliques"}]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/Iterator","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Inherited from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sequence.Iterator"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Cliques\/St","doc:\/\/Cliques\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Cliques\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/Iterator\/next()"]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/iterator"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Iterator"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]}],"references":{"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques":{"abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","title":"Cliques","type":"topic","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/cliques"},"doc://Cliques/s8SendableP":{"type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Sendable","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/s8SendableP"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques":{"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every maximal clique of an undirected graph’s simple graph once, lazily, each in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order (by vertex index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"degeneracy d."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques","kind":"symbol","title":"MaximalCliques","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques"},"doc://Cliques/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/s16SendableMetatypeP","type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.SendableMetatype"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques/Iterator/next()":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/Iterator\/next()","abstract":[],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"next"},{"kind":"